```

The `PUT_InsertContract` method verifies the preconditions are satisfied and conducts the insertion operation using the `Insert` method of `ArrayList`. Furthermore, it checks the new conditions after the insertion operation such as the count of the array, the index of `x`, the last index of `x`, and whether it contains `x`. 

To make sure that an item inserted at some location is in fact at the last position, the test case checks if `New_arrListLastIndexOf_x` is less than or equal to `Old_arrListCount`. 

We add `PexObserve.ValueForViewing` to display the values in test viewer for easy debugging. 

This function can be automatically tested by Pex testing tool. However, the current implementation only works in Pex UI mode, due to the complex nature of `Insensitive` attribute usage in `ArrayList`'s members. 

More advanced techniques like using custom data objects with interfaces, refraction, or Pex code contracts are needed for more comprehensive and robust functional testing in practice.--------------------            Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX <= Old_arrListCount, "Insertion into ArrayList should place the inserted item at this position if the ArrayList was not full");

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that index of x after insertion is less than or equal to old index of x
            Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX <= Old_arrListIndexOfX, "Insertion into ArrayList should place the inserted item at this position if the ArrayList was not full.");

            if (Old_arrListIndexOfX != -1) // Checking if the element already exists in the List
            {
                // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(\);" that New_arrListIndexOf_x is greater than or equal to old arrListIndexOf_x
                Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= Old_arrListIndexOfX, "Insertion into ArrayList should place the inserted item at this position if the ArrayList was not full.");
            }

        }
    }
}
```
To perform Pex testing, you may need to install the extension `Pex for Visual Studio 2017` from the marketplace on Visual Studio 2017. Once installed, right-click the solution and choose "Add -> Pex Tests".

Here are some notes:

1. It's important to note the preconditions - we assume the index provided is within the count bounds.

2. Last position of inserted object is less than or equal than original array count (since it has been inserted at the end of the array)

3. Index of the inserted object is less than or equal to the original index (if the object was already present in the ArrayList), and greater than or equal to the original index (if the object was not present in the ArrayList). This will ensure the array list maintains its ordering.

4. It also handles the case where the item was not present in the ArrayList and thus indexing starts from the end of the ArrayList (index is 0 or larger than last index).

5. Assertions are used to prove our assumptions. In this case, we assert that if the ArrayList had an old item, then the new ArrayList's index of the item is greater than the old ArrayList's index of the item, this is because the item was inserted after it in the original ArrayList.--------------------